        "explanation": "<p>Express as $\\frac{A}{x + 1} + \\frac{B}{x - 2}$. Multiply through by the denominator:<br>$3x + 5 = A(x - 2) + B(x + 1)$. Solve for $A$ and $B$ by substituting $x = -1$ and $x = 2$:<br>$A = -2$, $B = 5$. Thus, the partial fractions are $\\frac{-2}{x + 1} + \\frac{5}{x - 2}$.</p>",
